# Paths this repo never commits (bash globs, one per line; `*` also matches `/`). The pre-commit hook refuses
# any staged path that matches. These are the licensed data slice, the fixture trees, the trial transcripts and the
# private term lists (AGENTS.md "No git remote" and plans/PUBLIC_RELEASE.md say why).
#
# `issues/` (the planted-issue catalogue) is NOT listed on purpose: it is tracked today and new issues are committed
# there in the normal workflow, so a refusal would block it. Its removal from history is corsu Phase C (decision 10).
